---
import { withoutTrailingStop } from "../../../lib/typography";
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const source = (await getCollection("experiments")).find((item) => item.data.id === "experiment:city-orbit");
const href = source?.data.href;
const repo = source?.data.repo;
const updated = source?.data.updated ? new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric" }).format(source.data.updated) : "";
const description = "A street from OpenStreetMap becomes a hologram: select places with a ray, lift their cards and change the city radius with a gesture.";
const jsonLd = { "@type": "CreativeWork", "@id": new URL("/en/experiments/city-orbit/#content", Astro.site).href, url: new URL("/en/experiments/city-orbit/", Astro.site).href, name: "CITY//ORBIT", description, inLanguage: "en", author: { "@id": new URL("/#stanislav-ermolenko", Astro.site).href }, isPartOf: { "@id": new URL("/#website", Astro.site).href }, ...(source?.data.updated ? { dateModified: source.data.updated.toISOString() } : {}) };
---
<Base title="CITY//ORBIT" description={description} lang="en" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="entry-shell">
    <header class="entry-hero"><div class="entry-hero-meta"><span class="section-kicker">Experiment · Running</span></div><h1>CITY//ORBIT</h1><p class="entry-summary">{withoutTrailingStop(description)}</p><div class="publication-facts">{href && <a href={href}>Open experiment ↗</a>}{repo && <a href={repo}>Code ↗</a>}</div><dl class="work-facts"><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Art experience</dd></div><div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd>Headsets · mobile · desktop</dd></div><div><dt>Technology</dt><dd>{source?.data.stack.join(" · ")}</dd></div>{updated && <div><dt>Updated</dt><dd>{updated}</dd></div>}</dl></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The experience</h2><p>A real city contracts into a hologram between your hands. Named OpenStreetMap places become abstract points around a point called YOU: place the model on a table or unfold it 360° around yourself, without using ready-made 3D buildings.</p>
      <h2>Interaction</h2><ul><li><strong>TABLE</strong> places a 1.2-metre orbital model in front of you; <strong>360°</strong> surrounds you with it.</li><li>Select, pinch or click chooses a POI and lifts its card.</li><li>Two hands in pinch, spreading apart, change the radius: <strong>200 m → 1 km → 5 km</strong>.</li><li>Phone and desktop retain HTML controls and coordinates as a fallback.</li></ul>
      <h2>Data and limits</h2><p>The client makes bounded Overpass queries against public instances for named places. Results are session-cached and overloaded services enter cooldown. If the services do not answer, an explicitly labelled demo quarter near the Hermitage appears rather than being presented as live data. OpenStreetMap data © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.</p>
      <p>Google XR Blocks depends on WebXR. Required browser capabilities can be absent on iOS, including Safari, so this experiment may not start there. Quest 3 is the target platform; the desktop simulator is for testing the mechanics.</p>
      <h2>Links</h2><ul>{href && <li><a href={href}>Open the experience</a></li>}{repo && <li><a href={repo}>Source code</a></li>}</ul><p class="entry-original"><a class="text-link" href="/experiments/city-orbit/">Original (Russian) →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>